ss 1, Q3=100 m³/h\"). Attributes optional — I'll skip attributes since model_level covers them. Or include minimal attributes like {dn, accuracy_class, q3}. To keep the JSON manageable, I'll include model_id + label only.\n\nActually, maybe include attributes with nominal_diameter, accuracy_class, q3 for convenience. Hmm, that duplicates. I'll include just model_id and label.\n\nAlso type_designations for certified_type: [\"Sharpflow SWB7 + CWB7\", \"SWB7\", \"CWB7\"]? The document says Type: \"Sharpflow SWB7 + CWB7\". I'll list [\"Sharpflow SWB7 + CWB7\"] and put components separately with SWB7/CWB7. Actually \"all type/model identifiers mentioned\" — SWB7 and CWB7 are mentioned within the type string. I'll include all three: [\"Sharpflow SWB7 + CWB7\", \"Sharpflow SWB7\", \"CWB7\"]. Hmm, \"Sharpflow SWB7\" — is \"Sharpflow\" the brand for both? The type is \"Sharpflow SWB7 + CWB7\" so presumably SWB7 is \"Sharpflow SWB7\". I'll include \"SWB7\" and \"CWB7\" as bare designations in components and keep type_designations as the full string plus parts. Let me do: type_designations: [\"Sharpflow SWB7 + CWB7\", \"SWB7\", \"CWB7\"].\n\nCategory: \"Water meter\".\n\nModule designation: For R49 the modules concept isn't like R60's \"Analog load cell\". I'll set null or omit. Schema allows null. I'll omit (rule 8: omit if not present).\n\nDescription: combine page 1 and page 3 descriptions: \"Water meter intended for the metering of cold potable water and hot water, based on an electromagnetic principle, designed to measure forward and reverse flow, with (minimum) 0 D straight inlet and outlet, with no flow conditioner and equipped with an electronic calculating/indicating device. Class 1 and 2.\" I'll write a merged English description.\n\nRecommendation accuracy_classes: [\"1\",\"2\"].\n\nTest reports: roles — \"type_evaluation_report\" seems most apt for OIML conformity certificates (the associated test report = type evaluation report). The doc calls them \"Test Reports\". I'll use \"test_report\" as role. Dates unknown → omit. Pages: 41, 40, 40, 40.\n\nNote the fourth report: \"R49-1.2006-NL1-12.01\" — I'll transcribe as printed but it's likely a typo for \"R49-1/2006-NL1-12.01\". Rule: don't fabricate; transcribe. I'll keep \"R49-1.2006-NL1-12.01\". Hmm, risk either way. I'll keep as printed.\n\nNow the software_versions value: I'll use a string: \"4.0.4_; 4.0.10_; 4.0.11_; 4.0.12_; 4.2.2_\". In matrix rows same.\n\nIndicating range: 99999999 m³. I'll record type_level: {\"indicating_range\": {\"value\": 99999999, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"}}.\n\nTemperature: {\"min_max_admissible_temperature\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 50}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"}}.\n\nOrientation: {\"value\": \"All positions\"} — orientation isn't a quantity; unit null.\n\nEnvironmental class: {\"value\": \"C\"}.\n\nPower supply type: {\"value\": \"Battery\"}; battery_voltage_ub: {\"value\": 3.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}.\n\nLet me also consider max admissible pressure varies per model → model_level (already included).\n\nNow assemble matrix_tables. To keep the response size manageable but faithful, I'll include all five tables with all rows.\n\nTable 1 (page 3, class 1, DN65–DN125):\nrows:\n1. {model: \"DN65 class 1 Q3=100\", meter_size: \"DN65\", q1: 0.4, q2: 0.64, q3: 100, q4: 125, ratio_q3_q1: 250, nominal_diameter: 65, verification_scale_interval: 0.0001}\n2. {model: \"DN80 class 1 Q3=100\", meter_size: \"DN80\", q1: 0.625, q2: 1.0, q3: 100, q4: 125, ratio: 160, nd: 80, vsi: 0.0001}\n3. {model: \"DN80 class 1 Q3=160\", ..., q1: 0.64, q2: 1.02, q3: 160, q4: 200, ratio: 250, nd: 80, vsi: 0.0001}\n4. {model: \"DN100 class 1 Q3=160\", q1: 1.0, q2: 1.6, q3: 160, q4: 200, ratio: 160, nd: 100, vsi: 0.001}\n5. {model: \"DN100 class 1 Q3=250\", q1: 1.0, q2: 1.6, q3: 250, q4: 312.5, ratio: 250, nd: 100, vsi: 0.001}\n6. {model: \"DN125 class 1 Q3=250\", q1: 1.56, q2: 2.5, q3: 250, q4: 312.5, ratio: 160, nd: 125, vsi: 0.001}\n7. {model: \"DN125 class 1 Q3=400\